{{recipe}}

This jelly dessert uses agar as a thickener, making it suitable for vegetarians.

==Ingredients==
* {{convert|5|g|oz}} {{cb|agar}} powder
* {{convert|100|g|oz}} white granulated {{cb|sugar}}
* {{convert|500|g|oz}} {{cb|water}}
* {{convert|75|g|oz}} {{cb|milk}}
* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] {{cb|almond extract}}
* 6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] {{cb|fruit cocktail}}
* 150 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] (0.625 cups) {{cb|syrup}}

== Procedure ==
# Put agar, sugar, and water in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] and bring to [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. 
# Take off heat, and drain some of the water.
# When cool, add in milk and almond extract.
# Pour mixture into tin. 
# When completely cool, chill in the refrigerator for about 15 minutes until set.
# Cut almond jelly into cubes.
# Serve with fruit cocktail and syrup in a glass bowl.

